  "notes": "Synthetic. Truth is what each line does at run time, except where a policy turns a value into a gap: a value refused as a credential (credentials.py:41 sends the dict.get default `gpt-4`, but its lookup key is credential-shaped, so the call is a credential gap), a model chosen by a for clause (scopes.py:10) and a name assigned again after a deferred use (scopes.py:16) are gaps, not values. Gap `values` (the models a run-time lookup, a branch or the in-file callers may give) are triage hints and are not compared here; the unit tests check them. dicts.py:9, :14 and :24 expand dicts that are changed after they are written, so they are read as unknown `**kwargs`; dicts.py:38 is only read and resolves. env_endpoint.py sets OPENAI_BASE_URL, so the client built without a base_url is unknown with an endpoint_env gap and the one given a base_url stays custom_base_url. rerouted.py:11 is given a base_url after construction; rerouted.py:16 builds an AzureOpenAI or an OpenAI depending on the import, so its call is ambiguous and the construction is not listed as a client. params.py:33 is public, so its client default and its caller's gateway are both possible; params.py:40 is private and its only caller passes the gateway. params.py:50 resolves from its only caller but keeps an in_file_callers gap because send() is public; _send() at :54 does not. scopes.py:29 reads CL7 when the class body runs, before CL7 is rebound. scopes.py:39 and :42 are Track C h042: the client in each branch dominates its own call. amplify.py expands 40 nested fallbacks at each call: 32 are listed (one distinct value) and a truncated gap says more were cut. `gpt-3.5-turbo-instruct` is the module M that params.py:29 must not report, and `o4-mini` is what tweak() writes into a dict that must not be read. params.py:21 reports ask_quiet()'s default with a parameter_default gap: the function is public, so another module may pass another model (policy round)."
